{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/wasm/BUILD.bazel","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570Z","id":"dd6826e601091c10284caf7ad4074eb06597d6f31ede78fe71039d300b5988aa","body":{"detail":"ring's and sqlite-wasm-rs's build scripts compile with the Android NDK's clang and llvm-ar (bazel/wasm/c_tools.bzl). The NDK ships its prebuilt LLVM for macOS and x86-64 Linux only, and :ndk_clang, :ndk_llvm_ar and :ndk_llvm_files fall back to toolchains/llvm/prebuilt/linux-x86_64 on any other machine, so on aarch64 Linux the label does not exist and //crates/clax-worker:bundle and //bazel/wasm:check fail to analyse.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":33},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"ecf51877389afbf334c24d49b5ec58dcd5757eccebb20fa31fba4a23688ad953"},"suggested_fix":"Fetch an LLVM release with a wasm32 backend for aarch64 Linux by checksum and select it there, or mark the wasm targets incompatible with that exec platform.","summary":"On a Linux arm64 machine the Worker's wasm32 C has no compiler","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/wasm/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570044Z","id":"1f5cf1f586742de52ef06cab286a5e5cf862a6e0c9dfa1c15263a6b7db9e2fc3","body":{"detail":"//crates/clax-worker:bundle, //bazel/wasm:check and the wrangler and browser tests over the bundle (crates/clax-worker/BUILD.bazel) passed on an Apple silicon Mac. On CI's Ubuntu runner they use the NDK's linux-x86_64 LLVM, wasm-bindgen's x86_64-unknown-linux-musl build, binaryen's x86_64-linux wasm-opt and esbuild's linux-x64 (bazel/wasm/tools.MODULE.bazel), and workerd's Linux package; none of those has run here. The first CI run of the bazel job is the first Linux build.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":43},"end":{"line":62},"content_hash":"832053acfe58ebd54cda436554667be6107cf1203c7b0ab835c5204ecf7d336d"},"summary":"The Worker's bundle and its wasm32 C have been built only on macOS","tags":["session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/wasm/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570148Z","id":"09f3dbaf160e81b6837403b5b68111a2f1bc6349d8a5fd8159ade2a8697666aa","body":{"detail":"crate_universe builds a path crate's repository over its source directory and writes its generated BUILD.bazel there: a trial with clax-worker and clax-do-vfs as path specs overwrote the BUILD.bazel of the 17 workspace crates they reach (restored from git). So the specs name every third-party crate the Worker's build reaches with Cargo's features (scripts/bazel-derive.py wasm-specs) and no workspace crate.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":31},"end":{"line":33},"content_hash":"efe0752af211f898fca1cec021a4904386758433547e2247fc643b5de40f69fb"},"summary":"Resolve @crates_wasm from crate.spec(path = ...) of the Worker's crates rather than one spec per third-party crate","tags":["build","revisit:crate_universe stops writing BUILD files into a path crate's source directory","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"bazel/wasm/README.md","issuer":"mailto:alex@kesling.co","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-28T20:06:10.570172Z","id":"d4238f6e450f5032d5f2004c234455ba243b672b9e456026ba1e657d36c5843e","body":{"detail":"Gating would keep tokio's full, reqwest's blocking and the rest off wasm32, but crate_universe keys a proc macro's features by the host it runs on, merged across every platform it builds for: with wasm32 added to @crates, rmcp-macros took the `local` that clax-mcp turns on for wasm32 only, and the native clax_mcp failed to compile (34 errors, its tools' futures no longer Send). A universe of its own for wasm32 (@crates_wasm) avoids both.","kind":"alternative","span":{"start":{"line":9},"end":{"line":23},"content_hash":"18f53c3843ccd39c65949fba88827cb57bcbcc4725fc9228d83d6d5554e88591"},"summary":"One crate universe for native and wasm32, the daemon's native-only dependencies gated behind cfg(not(target_family = \"wasm\"))","tags":["build","revisit:crate_universe keys a proc macro's features by the target platform it is built for","session:claude-code:02ec6080-e7bb-4940-94c1-2f7bed23b002"]}}
